liblocation without location-ui, location-control and MCE (FreeBSD's
Hildon has none of them):

- location-ui shows the disclaimer and the "enable positioning" dialogs
  and answers with a "response" signal. Without it (the service unknown)
  the start ended in "System error"; now the dialog's yes is taken: the
  disclaimer accepted (stored in GConf as by the dialog), GPS and network
  positioning on.
- location-control (the settings applet) sets the device in GConf's
  method pair; with none set, the internal receiver ("las": gpsd through
  location-daemon) instead of a Bluetooth receiver, which needed BlueZ.
- MCE's get_device_mode tells flight and offline mode, in which liblocation
  restricts the methods. Without MCE the device mode is "normal".

